          "id": "SP_NEPHASOMA_COLUMBARIS_KAWAUCHI_RICE_2009",
          "name": "Nephasoma columbaris Kawauchi & Rice, 2009",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Nephasoma",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p>External morphology: Holdfast papillae have a round shape. The larger (80-300 µm) ones have a hardened anterior margin usually appearing as a thin, pale border, which occasionally extends around the entire margin. Hooks are type I, slightly bent, spinelike (30-90 µm tall). Tentacular crown consists of 20-30 tentacles. Internal anatomy: Dorsal and ventral retractor muscles (DRM and VRM) are of equal size and originate at the end of the trunk. DRM has one origin and VRM may have one but usually shows two origins. Esophagus attaches to the VRM. Intestine consists of one or two loops plus the spiral. (From Stephen and Edmonds, 1972; Cutler and Cutler, 1985; Cutler, 1994)</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:6107344"
