          "id": "SP_GOLFINGIA_MURICAUDATA",
          "name": "Golfingia muricaudata",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Golfingia",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(EMU- 13446) Trunk 50 mm in length; rough, light brown body wall; scattered thin, cylindrical papillae. Caudal appendage 10 % of trunk length, covered with cylindrical papillae. Introvert incomplete, shorter than trunk. Longitudinal musculature continuous. Four retractor muscles (RM), dorsal RM attached to body wall anteriorly to ventral pair and more separated from ventral nerve cord. Esophagus attached to ventral RM. Two sack-shaped nephridia; nephridiopores open anteriorly anus; without spindle muscle; rectum with six thin lateral muscles; ventral nerve cord ends before internal anterior margin of caudal appendage. Habitat Bathyal (1045 m); muddy sand bottom.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2509842"
